## data/control-vectors/lora-out exclusion added 2026-09-13 -- these are    ##
## trained-model reference artifacts (adapter_config.json, tokenizer.       ##
## json, etc), not source. exclusion patterns in @copy_sources apply even   ##
## when update-signatures is handed an EXPLICIT file list [ e.g.  the       ##
## staged set during a commit ] -- that path bypasses this file's own       ##
## INCLUSION globs entirely and signs any named file that exists, so only   ##
## an exclusion here actually stops it. caught live: a signed               ##
## adapter_config.json/tokenizer.json gets an AMOS7 footer appended after   ##
## the closing JSON, breaking any strict `json.load()` on it [ had to strip ##
## a temp copy before every GGUF conversion this session ];                 ##
## adapter_model.safetensors is a strict length-checked format that flatly  ##
## refuses to load at all once a footer is appended -- the .safetensors     ##
## half is already gitignored [ base.source.collect_file_ list filters      ##
## staged paths through git check-ignore ], but the small json/tokenizer    ##
## files ARE deliberately tracked in git [ real, useful reference           ##
## artifacts, same as the first lora attempt's adapter ] and were never     ##
## excluded from signing specifically until now                             ##
##                                                                          ##
## data/control-vectors/results exclusion added same session, same reason:  ##
## the raw generation-response json files run_gens.sh/run_gens_ lora.sh     ##
## save (results/ and results-lora/, matched by the same substring since    ##
## "results-lora" begins with "results") were ALSO getting signed --        ##
## score.py's own json.load() on a signed response file would break the     ##
## same way lora_to_gguf.py's did on a signed adapter_config.json           ##

if ( not chdir(<system.root_path>) ) {
    <[base.s_warn]>
        ->( ': cannot change workdir to : %s', <system.root_path> );
    return undef;
} else {

    return <[base.source.collect_file_list]>->( \@copy_sources );
}

